// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// specs/t27os/update_probe.t27 -- a program that shows update_core.t27 + update_host.t27 working (Refs gHashTag/t27#11560).
// Headless, NOT the app: T27OS.app is never started. Prints one line per fact; the lines say what was OBSERVED.
// UP_ROLE (default table):
//   table     in memory (no ~/.t27os is read or written): two throw-away identities, a 2 MiB test file in $UP_DIR (default
//             /tmp): make a manifest, sign it, check it; flip one byte of every region; a stranger; a forged signature
//             under a friend's key; a rollback (build-1 and the same build); a size out of range; a truncated manifest; the
//             file hash and size; a second start while an update runs. Prints the table CASE | EXPECT | GOT.
//   announce  open (or make) the identity under $HOME/.t27os, register _t27call._udp with TXT fp/port/nick + ver/build, keep
//             it for UP_SECONDS. Run it with HOME=<an empty temp directory>.
//   browse    browse _t27call._udp for UP_SECONDS, resolve what is found and print each service with ver= and build= read
//             from its TXT record, and whether it runs a newer build than UP_BUILD.
//   both      announce and browse in one process.
//   xfer      part 2, on this machine only (127.0.0.1): makes small fake .app bundles under $UP_XDIR (default
//             /tmp/updtest; it is emptied first), zips them with ditto, and for each case starts a second process of this
//             program as the server (UP_ROLE=serve), then downloads, checks and installs into $UP_XDIR/inst/T27OS.app as
//             the app would: success, a flipped byte, a cut connection resumed in the same run and in a later run, a
//             stranger's manifest, a lower build, a bundle of another app, a build that fails its health check after the
//             swap, a failed rename, a busy lock, a request for a bundle the server does not have. Prints
//             CASE | EXPECT | GOT and what is live after each case. Never touches T27OS.app or ~/.t27os.
//   offer     a neighbour with a newer build for the app under test: UP_APP (a .app), HOME of that app (same identity),
//             UP_SECONDS (120), UP_NAME (upd-probe), UP_EXPECT=1 wants one whole bundle sent. See up_offer.
//   lock      the lock next to an app (/tmp/t27uh-lock-test.app.lock): taken with this pid, kept while its owner runs,
//             kept for 10 minutes after its owner died, removed after that (uh_lock_sweep), released only by its owner.
//   serve     the server half of xfer (started by it): UP_SRV_M (manifest file), UP_SRV_ZIP (bundle), UP_SRV_READY
//             (file made once listening), UP_CUT_AT / UP_FLIP_AT (test aids, 0 = off), UP_PORT, UP_SECONDS.
// UP_SECONDS (default 8), UP_PORT (default 47741; xfer and serve: 47790), UP_NICK (default t27os), UP_NAME (instance name, default the nick),
// UP_VERSION as a.b.c (default 0.1.3), UP_BUILD (default 4321), UP_DIR (default /tmp).
// Exit 0 only when every check this role makes passed.
// Build (Apple silicon):
//   t27b build specs/t27os/update_probe.t27 -o up.o --macho
//   ld -arch arm64 -platform_version macos 11.0 $(xcrun --show-sdk-version) -syslibroot $(xcrun --show-sdk-path) \
//      -e _main -lSystem -lffi -framework CoreFoundation -framework Security -o update_probe up.o
